{"title":"1955 AHSME Problems/Problem 50","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1955_AHSME_Problems/Problem_50&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In order to pass <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> going <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/7/78792fe4680a164f537ea72a4f900e4471433c3b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$40$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> mph on a two-lane highway, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />, going <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/6/906734e2f1010e9a171ffee8050cbc0649cea37c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$50$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> mph, must gain <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/1/651ba418a810d971dbc8a326d49a71fe1541fae0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$30$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> feet. \nMeantime, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/2/2b2552a7bb2b15a631fadffa51042c8c9d1a30f4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C, 210$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"48\" height=\"16\" /> feet from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />, is headed toward him at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/6/906734e2f1010e9a171ffee8050cbc0649cea37c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$50$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> mph. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> maintain their speeds, \nthen, in order to pass safely, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> must increase his speed by: \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/f/2afb96c491c978cef249d79a9aed73f605428c83.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ \\text{30 mph}\\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ \\text{10 mph}\\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ \\text{5 mph}\\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ \\text{15 mph}\\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ \\text{3 mph}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"559\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1955_AHSME_Problems/Problem_50&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/2/b12a2029af5adb9b22d052cf2cf68597fcc1569e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$V_A, V_B, V_C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"83\" height=\"18\" /> be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/9/299ddf7c0f03ea46bf09f81f93adeea0756aa15c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A, B, C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"58\" height=\"16\" />'s velocity, respectively. We want to pass <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> before we collide with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> are going in the same direction and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/8/7885290406ee72a7ceaa02781e49a9879af72bfa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$V_A&gt;V_B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"70\" height=\"17\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> will pass <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/a/2dab869ee403866dde051206fb82ef706a7275e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{30\\mathrm{ft}}{V_A-V_B}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"71\" height=\"42\" /> time. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> are going in opposite directions, their relative velocity is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57e54e0d9977709a50436401d290ca3f0e0706f1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$V_A+V_C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"67\" height=\"17\" />, so the amount of time before <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> will collide with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is given by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/4/e840853b8609a3c230405e660c4dde7933babbff.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{210\\mathrm{ft}}{V_A+V_C}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"71\" height=\"42\" />. We want to pass <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> before we collide with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/d/4cd875e0fbb8f87b150b3cc759135b0e27f1a670.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$V_A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"23\" height=\"17\" /> must satisfy the inequality <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/5/ef571d19876167df7f3754db6099408d8a28fccb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{30\\mathrm{ft}}{V_A-V_B}&lt;\\frac{210\\mathrm{ft}}{V_A+V_C}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"165\" height=\"42\" />. We can eliminate all the units, simplifying the inequality to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/5/76554c811c437e40889988921f63dcc2fa203f10.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{V_A-V_B} &lt; \\frac{7}{V_A+V_C}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"165\" height=\"41\" />. Solving this and substituting our known values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/d/45d1386fd135df774421ec609fe1f5e891850478.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$V_B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"24\" height=\"17\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/7/2e7f425547b24e641c8007bb92e86b02931736ec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$V_C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"20\" height=\"15\" /> yields <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/e/b7e16bed2781e26bb9f7fc07f83a1de79b62e1f8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$330&lt;6V_A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"84\" height=\"17\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> must increase his speed by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/e/e3e5945b9c62fd9a5ae2532e9ca0f9b2d640d492.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(C) \\ } 5 }$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"64\" height=\"30\" /> miles per hour.\n</p><p>~anduran\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017024556\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.013 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.021 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 143/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 0/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 2/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 6903/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    0.000      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:26620:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017024556 and revision id 291049. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}